ng_hci: answer SCO and eSCO requests with the synchronous commands

Accept_Connection_Request must not answer an eSCO request, and gives a
SCO request only the controller's voice setting. Answer every
synchronous Connection_Request with Accept_Synchronous_Connection_Request
(CVSD from 16-bit linear PCM, 64 kbit/s, any latency, every packet
type) or Reject_Synchronous_Connection_Request, from ng_hci_sync.c (this
directory's src/). Every controller since Bluetooth 1.2 takes these.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#237). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_ulpi.c

--- a/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_ulpi.c
+++ b/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_ulpi.c
